*  STEP 4 witness (kw-missing-4): &FILE standalone.
*  &FILE names the CURRENT statement's file, so unlike &LASTFILE no leading statement is needed
*  before the read -- it is readable from the program's very first statement.
*  It answers the source path AS INVOKED, so this witness reports only the BASENAME TAIL: a bare
*  path .ref would change with the caller's cwd and could not be pinned.
        f = &FILE
        f ('k32_file_keyword.sno' RPOS(0))                                     :S(ok)F(bad)
ok      OUTPUT = 'file-tail=OK'                                                :(fin)
bad     OUTPUT = 'file-tail=BAD'
fin
END
